[00:31.020 --> 00:40.360]  There's a sense of being there, the do-iness of this morning, the wetness, the heaviness of the moisture on the trees.
[00:40.360 --> 00:51.920]  Scholars still debate whether this freely brushed painting was intended as a preparatory sketch for one of Constable's six-foot landscapes, or whether he considered it finished in itself.
[00:52.440 --> 01:03.380]  I tend to think it really is finished, because everything is there, and it's also beautifully harmonized. It's also just an incredibly moving painting.
[01:03.380 --> 01:21.580]  It is such a nondescript place, and yet somehow he ennobles it with the size of the painting, but also in this incredible interest in the way the atmosphere impacts on this landscape at that time.
